# sha256 of every stock hook this installer has EVER shipped. A repo whose hook is one of these
# has never been edited locally -- it is simply on an older stock -- and install.sh overwrites
# it without --force. Before this list existed, three repos that had never touched their hooks
# were refused as "locally modified" the day the stock hook changed (2026-09-21), because the
# install record did not exist yet on hooks installed before the record did. Append, never
# remove: a hash removed from here turns a pristine old install back into a refusal.
